---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionMark from '../../components/SectionMark.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Prashant Kumar" description="About Prashant Kumar and his work across enterprise strategy, architecture, AI and transformation.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-identity"><SectionMark kind="about" size="md" tone="blue" /><p class="eyebrow">About</p></div>
      <h1>I work where strategy meets<br/>architecture and delivery.</h1>
      <p class="lede">My work sits at the intersection of enterprise strategy and architecture — modernising complex technology estates, navigating major technology choices and harnessing AI responsibly while balancing resilience, regulation, cost and long-term optionality.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--roomy">
    <div class="container brand-columns">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How I think</p>
        <h2>Clarity before certainty.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lead-copy">I am most useful when the problem crosses organisational and technology boundaries — where there is no perfect answer, the consequences matter, and a decision still has to be made.</p>
        <p>I value evidence, reversible decisions, practical experimentation and architecture that survives contact with delivery. I am less interested in prescribing a perfect future than in helping organisations preserve the ability to adapt as the future changes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Current themes</p>
        <div><h2>What I’m exploring now.</h2><p>The themes below increasingly overlap. That intersection — not any single technology — is where I think the most interesting enterprise architecture questions are emerging.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="focus-grid">
        <article class="focus-card"><span>01</span><h3>AI-native enterprise architecture</h3><p>How architecture changes when models and agents become participants in delivery and operations.</p></article>
        <article class="focus-card"><span>02</span><h3>Data, events & interoperability</h3><p>Creating durable enterprise foundations that support customer journeys, AI and multiple channels without unnecessary coupling.</p></article>
        <article class="focus-card"><span>03</span><h3>Platform optionality</h3><p>Capturing SaaS speed while retaining control of strategic data, intelligence, integration and future choices.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section reading-now">
    <div class="container reading-now-grid">
      <div class="reading-now-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Currently reading</p>
        <h2>What is shaping<br/>my thinking now.</h2>
        <p>A small, changing selection of ideas I am reading — not as endorsements, but as useful provocations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="reading-now-list">
        <article>
          <span>01</span>
          <div><h3>Laws of Software Engineering</h3><p class="book-author">Dr Milan Milanović</p><p>A compact vocabulary for the forces that shape software systems, teams and the decisions around them.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>02</span>
          <div><h3>AI Demystified</h3><p class="book-author">Antonio Weiss</p><p>A pragmatic bridge between AI’s technical possibility and the choices leaders need to make at work.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span>03</span>
          <div><h3>Orchestrating Experiences</h3><p class="book-author">Chris Risdon &amp; Patrick Quattlebaum</p><p>Exploring how fragmented organisations can align people, channels and systems around coherent experiences.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section speaking-section">
    <div class="container speaking-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Speaking & conversations</p>
        <h2>Ideas are better<br/>when spoken aloud.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="speaking-copy">
        <p class="lead-copy">I enjoy speaking about enterprise architecture, AI, digital transformation and the choices organisations face when technology moves faster than governance.</p>
        <p>I’ve spoken at architecture community meetups and internal forums, and I’m always interested in thoughtful industry conversations, panels and conference sessions where I can contribute something useful.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="mailto:hello@kumarprashant.net?subject=Speaking%20invitation">Invite me to speak →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="quote-section">
    <div class="container quote-grid">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Why the Lab exists</p>
      <blockquote>Small working experiments make abstract architecture arguments visible.</blockquote>
      <p class="quote-note">The Architecture Lab is where I test ideas in public, learn by building and turn technology curiosity into evidence.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .reading-now-grid,
    .speaking-grid {
      display:grid;
      grid-template-columns:.72fr 1.28fr;
      gap:90px;
      align-items:start;
    }
    .reading-now-intro h2,
    .speaking-grid h2 { font-size:clamp(36px,4vw,48px); line-height:1.08; }
    .reading-now-intro > p:last-child { max-width:390px; margin:24px 0 0; color:var(--muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.7; }
    .reading-now-list { border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
    .reading-now-list article { display:grid; grid-template-columns:42px 1fr; gap:24px; padding:28px 0; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
    .reading-now-list article > span { padding-top:4px; color:var(--amber); font-size:11px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.14em; }
    .reading-now-list h3 { margin:0; font:400 25px/1.2 Georgia,serif; }
    .book-author { margin:6px 0 12px !important; color:var(--blue) !important; font-size:11px !important; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
    .reading-now-list article div > p:last-child { max-width:620px; margin:0; color:var(--muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.65; }
    .speaking-copy .lead-copy { margin:0 0 20px; font:400 25px/1.5 Georgia,serif; }
    .speaking-copy > p:not(.lead-copy) { max-width:680px; margin:0 0 26px; color:var(--muted); font-size:15px; line-height:1.72; }
    @media (max-width:900px) {
      .reading-now-grid,
      .speaking-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:44px; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
